@model WorkshopModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Request identity"; }
<h1>Change the request, not a singleton.</h1><p class="lead">Demo presets supply claims and browser headers only to the workshop. They never grant dashboard access.</p>
<section class="card"><h2>Choose a demo request</h2><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/identity?preset=matching">Matching · Alice</a><a class="button secondary" href="/identity?preset=nonmatching">Non-matching · Bob</a></div><dl><dt>Identity.Name</dt><dd>@Model.Persona.Name</dd><dt>role claim</dt><dd>@Model.Persona.Role</dd><dt>group claim</dt><dd>@(Model.Persona.Preset == "matching" ? "beta-testers" : "none")</dd><dt>filter-targeting</dt><dd>@(Model.Flags["filter-targeting"] ? "ON" : "OFF")</dd></dl></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Keep identity stable</h2><p><code>HttpContextTargetingContextAccessor</code> reads <code>User.Identity.Name</code> and literal <code>group</code> claims from the current request. Alice and Bob do not overwrite shared user state. Presets are query parameters, not credentials, sessions or production authentication.</p><p>Percentage rollout is sticky to the feature and identity. A 50% rule does not promise every other request, nor that Alice must be on and Bob off. Preserve the same accessor and identifiers when migrating to SaaS.</p></section>
